# eephus.io MLB Scores job (tools/scores_job.py). Install on the production box
# with `crontab -e` as the deploy user.
#
# NOT YET. Install this only AFTER the fWAR label epoch's step Z is recorded and
# AFTER the SCORES_LIVE flip (SCORES_5a_LIVE_FLIP) has reached the box
# (SCORES_PLAN.md section 17; deploy/WEBMASTER.md section 10 lists the steps in
# order). While scores_core.SCORES_LIVE is False the job writes only
# .cache/scores/preview/ whatever EEPHUS_SCORES_OUT says, so a line installed
# early serves nothing.
#
# BEFORE THIS LINE: the webmaster has created /opt/eephus/scores and added the
# nginx location in deploy/README.md ("MLB Scores: the /data/scores/ location").
#
# Not a betting job: public StatsAPI only, no key, no pricer, no Odds API credit,
# so it does not source /etc/eephus.env. Every 2 minutes, ALL DAY, and the job
# decides: live games every 2 to 3 minutes, otherwise every 30 minutes, the
# 7-day schedule once per UTC day at or after 10:00, every 6 hours in the
# offseason. `decide()` does all of its clock reasoning on UTC instants, so the
# line is correct under any box timezone; TZ=UTC keeps the log stamps in the same
# clock.
#
# flock -n drops an invocation that would overlap the previous one (the job also
# takes its own OS lock on .cache/scores/job.lock, released when it exits). The
# job never touches the nightly's lock, and it holds itself (exit 0, action
# epoch_hold) while ../_pre_epoch_fwar_2026-10/ exists without a step Z entry.
#
# ORDERING, READ THIS IF YOU PASTE BOTH EXAMPLES INTO ONE CRONTAB: crontab
# variable lines apply to every line AFTER them. deploy/betting-crontab.example
# sets EEPHUS=/opt/eephus/prospect-tracker, which is NOT the checkout the nightly
# uses (/opt/eephus/repo/prospect-tracker, deploy/nightly-build.sh). Paste this
# block AFTER the betting lines so its own EEPHUS line wins for the scores line,
# or fix the betting file's value too.
#
# AFTER INSTALLING, once one cycle has run:
#   cd /opt/eephus/repo/prospect-tracker && $PY tools/scores_job.py --selfcheck
#   curl -sI -A "Mozilla/5.0" https://eephus.io/data/scores/latest.json
#     (expect 200 and cache-control: no-cache)

SHELL=/bin/bash
TZ=UTC                                          # <- every line below is UTC
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
EEPHUS=/opt/eephus/repo/prospect-tracker        # <- the checkout the nightly uses
PY=/opt/eephus/venv/bin/python                  # <- the interpreter with the deps

*/2 * * * *  cd $EEPHUS && EEPHUS_SCORES_OUT=/opt/eephus/scores EEPHUS_WEBROOT=/var/www/eephus.io flock -n /tmp/eephus-scores.lock $PY tools/scores_job.py >> logs/scores-job.log 2>&1
